//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// apu_mix.v - the NES's non-linear mixer, as two lookup tables.
//
// GENERATED by the block at the top of this file's history -- see tools note in
// docs/ROADMAP.md. Do not hand-edit; regenerate.
//
// The channels do not simply add. Each group drives a resistor ladder into one
// node, so each extra unit of volume counts for less as the total rises. The
// two published closed forms are
//
//   pulse = 95.52  / (8128  / (p1 + p2) + 100)
//   tnd   = 163.67 / (24329 / (3*tri + 2*noise + dmc) + 100)
//
// and both are evaluated here at build time rather than as a divide per sample.
// Getting this wrong is not subtle: a linear sum makes everything too loud the
// moment more than one channel plays, which is most of the time.
//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

`default_nettype none

